<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  DeepDesertTribes.xml                    Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 4, "Deep Desert Tribes ; PATCH vanilla
  `TribeCivil`". A reskin, not a new def, plus the ONE group maker the spec
  explicitly orders added.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Misc.xml

      ParentName                  TribeBase
      OWN nodes                   defName · label · description · colorSpectrum ·
                                  disallowedMemes · maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation ·
                                  configurationListOrderPriority
      label                       gentle tribe

  🔴 EVERYTHING ELSE IS ON THE ABSTRACT PARENT, NOT ON THIS DEF.
  `TribeBase` carries `pawnSingular`, `pawnsPlural`, `leaderTitle`,
  `settlementGenerationWeight` and all twelve `pawnGroupMakers`.
  PatchOperations run BEFORE def inheritance is resolved, so `TribeCivil` has
  none of those nodes at patch time and a `Replace` on any of them matches ZERO
  and logs red. They are `Add`s onto the child. The child's own node wins at
  inheritance, so the override reaches `TribeCivil` ALONE ; patching `TribeBase`
  would also hit TribeRough, TribeSavage and every modded descendant.

      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  parent      ->  Add
      leaderTitle                 parent      ->  Add
      settlementGenerationWeight  parent (1)  ->  Add
      label / description         own nodes   ->  Replace
      permanentEnemy              ABSENT in the whole chain, so already false

  ⚠️ The spec's `permanentEnemy false` is the vessel's default and the reskin
  contract writes that field "only where it differs from the vessel's default".
  `TribeBase` and `TribeCivil` both omit it, and `TribeSavageBase` is a
  DIFFERENT parent. So nothing is written; the field is already false.

  ⛔ `factionNameMaker` and the raid curves are untouched.

  THE WATER RAID  (the one sanctioned group addition)
  ==================================================
  Vanilla lists twelve group makers on `TribeBase` and the child inherits them.
  RimWorld's inheritance MERGES `li` lists: the child's items are APPENDED to
  the parent's unless the node carries `Inherit="False"`. Verified against
  vanilla's own defs, e.g. `HoldingPlatform` adds one `<comps>` li to
  `HoldingPlatformBase`'s three and ends up with four, while
  `Horaxian_Gunner` has to write `Inherit="False"` on `weaponTags` precisely
  because appending is the default.

  ⇒ Adding a `<pawnGroupMakers>` node holding ONE `li` gives `TribeCivil`
  thirteen groups, not one. The twelve inherited ones are not touched and no
  commonality is rewritten.

  ⚠️ "Targets containers, disengages once loaded" is a RAID STRATEGY and an
  arrival mode, and a `pawnGroupMaker` expresses NEITHER. What a group maker
  can express is composition and size, so the signature is carried by those:
  `maxTotalPoints` 800 caps it to a light party (vanilla precedent, the
  Drifter group at 1000), and the options are the three FAST, LIGHT tribal
  kinds only. No `Tribal_HeavyArcher`, no `Tribal_Breacher`, no chiefs ; a
  breacher is the exact opposite of a group that leaves once it has the water.
  Commonality 30 against the parent's 100/60/60/5.

  Every kind here is vanilla Core and was checked present in the 2026-08-14
  dump, so no `MayRequire` is owed and none carries the 99999 exclude sentinel.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so the file is a
  silent no-op rather than a wall of red if the vessel ever moves.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "gentle tribe" -> the campaign name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Deep Desert Tribes</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>Territorial clans of the deep sand and the canyon country, for whom water is sacred and moisture farming is sacrilege — a theft from the world, committed in the open, every hour of every day.\n\nThey arrive fast, hit hard, and are gone.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Inherited from TribeBase. Add, not Replace. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>Tusken raider</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>Tusken raiders</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <!-- "chief" on the parent -> War Chief. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>War Chief</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 on the parent -> 1.3. Nine settlements, deep desert and canyons. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>1.3</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!-- The water raid. Appended to TribeBase's twelve, not replacing them. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <pawnGroupMakers>
              <li>
                <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
                <commonality>30</commonality>
                <maxTotalPoints>800</maxTotalPoints>
                <options>
                  <Tribal_Hunter>10</Tribal_Hunter>
                  <Tribal_Archer>8</Tribal_Archer>
                  <Tribal_Warrior>4</Tribal_Warrior>
                </options>
              </li>
            </pawnGroupMakers>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          faction_religions_spec.md entry 4 (B54)
          ================================================================
          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim; they are the only strings
          the engine renders. ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET or the
          description is never shown. Structure meme goes FIRST in
          `forcedMemes`.

          🔴 `TribeCivil` ships `disallowedMemes` = Supremacist · PainIsVirtue ·
          Nudism · Raider · Blindsight — and this faith FORCES both `Raider` and
          `PainIsVirtue`. Forcing a meme the same def disallows is a direct
          contradiction, so the node is removed rather than edited.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]/disallowedMemes</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>true</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>the Sun-Debt</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>The sun lends and the sand collects. Every mouthful you drink is borrowed, and the interest is paid in walking, in thirst, and in the marks we cut to remember the walking. A machine that pulls water out of the air is a thief standing between us and what we owe — it does not steal the water, it steals the debt. We take back what was drawn. We never take more than was drawn.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li>Structure_Animist</li>
              <li>NaturePrimacy</li>
              <li>Raider</li>
              <li MayRequire="vanillaquestsexpanded.generator">VQE_Technophobia</li>
              <li>PainIsVirtue</li>
            </forcedMemes>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Bespoke world-map icon. the def does NOT write it - it inherits Expanding/Village from TribeBase, so ADD.
             A Replace here would match nothing and log nothing. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="TribeCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><factionIconPath>World/JawaFactions/DeepDesertTribes</factionIconPath></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
